    "body": "@annevk \r\n\r\n> Patch https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#custom-element-reactions to mention that the callback can be passed an argument (unless the parent is removed as well).\r\n\r\nabout that last part, passing the argument conditionally sounds weird, why not always passing the parent? ultimately, if the parent is disconnected already (happens before the child is disconnected), there are still cases where you want to reach out to it. Otherwise we will end up with something like:\r\n\r\n```js\r\ndisconnectedCallback(parentOrUndefined) {\r\n    const parentNode = parentOrUndefined || this.parentNode;\r\n    // run the disconnecting sequence to break out with your parentNode\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe inverse (always passing it) is also true:\r\n\r\n```js\r\ndisconnectedCallback(parentNode) {\r\n    if (this.parentNode !== null) {\r\n        // run the disconnecting sequence to break out with your parentNode (if the parent is still there)\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n```",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
