    "created_at": "2019-05-21T07:19:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-05-21T07:19:41Z",
    "body": "In WebKit's builtin elements, we always pass in the parent node under which a subtree was removed or inserted. Since many callee are interested in updating its internal tree references upon removal or insertion so it's crucial that ancestor node from which a subtree was disconnected is given regardless of the removal had happened at its immediate parent or not.\r\n\r\nThat works okay because the callee can determine whether its immediate parent was removed or not by checking to see if the node has a parent (if it does, then its ancestor had been removed) since the callback is synchronous. Since custom elements' callbacks aren't fully synchronous, we may need to provide that information.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
